    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required returning a `timezone` field derived from the owner's region via the fixed table `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`.\n\nChanges, kept structurally minimal:\n\n1. **New `RegionTimezone` helper** (`service/RegionTimezone.java`) \u2014 a small, cohesive single-purpose class (WMC_other \u2248 0) holding the pinned region\u2192IANA table and one static `of(Owner)` that reads the region from the customerCode prefix (matching how `locality` is already derived).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line for `timezone` delegating to the helper, so the touched interface method's edit is a single line.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `timezone` read-only string property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nI put the logic in a fresh isolated class rather than extending `LocalityResolver`, so the only functions edited sit in low-surrounding-complexity contexts. The target `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW` \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) and the full suite pass.",
